  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nLocation: UniswapPriceOracle.validatePrice(uint256)\n\n`validatePrice()` is meant to compare the current spot price to a time-weighted average price (TWAP) derived from Uniswap V2 cumulative prices. In the current implementation, the “TWAP” calculation is built using the same spot price that is being validated, so the average becomes identical to the spot price whenever `elapsedTime > 0`\n\nIn `validatePrice()`:\n1) `tradePrice` is computed from current reserves via `getPrice()`.\n2) `cumulativePrice` is computed as `cumulativePriceLast + tradePrice * elapsedTime`.\n3) `timeWeightedAverage` is computed as `(cumulativePrice - cumulativePriceLast) / elapsedTime`, which becomes exactly `tradePrice` for any `elapsedTime > 0`.\n4) `derivation` becomes 0, so `validatePrice(0)` still returns true.\n\nConcretely, the function reads the pair’s last cumulative price, computes `tradePrice` from current reserves via `getPrice()`, then constructs a new cumulative value by adding `tradePrice * elapsedTime`. The subsequent “average” is computed as `(cumulativePrice - cumulativePriceLast) / elapsedTime`, which simplifies back to `tradePrice`. Because of that, the difference between `tradePrice` and the computed average is 0, and the slippage check passes even if the pool price was heavily manipulated between blocks.\n\n```js\nuint256 tradePrice = getPrice();\nuint256 cumulativePrice = cumulativePriceLast + (tradePrice * elapsedTime);\nuint256 timeWeightedAverage = (cumulativePrice - cumulativePriceLast) / elapsedTime;\nuint256 derivation = (tradePrice > timeWeightedAverage)\n    ? ((tradePrice - timeWeightedAverage) * 1e16) / timeWeightedAverage\n    : ((timeWeightedAverage - tradePrice) * 1e16) / timeWeightedAverage;\nreturn derivation <= slippage;\n```\n\nAs a result, any contract that relies on `validatePrice(0)` (or any small slippage) as a manipulation-resistance gate can still be executed at attacker-controlled prices, since the oracle check does not meaningfully constrain price movement.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nReplace the current approach with an actual TWAP based on two cumulative observations taken at different timestamps.",
  "proof_of_concept": "Create new file in `test/` and run with:\n```js\nforge test --match-test testValidatePriceTwapCollapsesToSpot\n```\n\n```js\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"../contracts/oracles/UniswapPriceOracle.sol\";\n\ncontract MockUniswapV2 is IUniswapV2 {\n    address internal _token0;\n    uint112 internal _reserve0;\n    uint112 internal _reserve1;\n    uint32 internal _blockTimestampLast;\n\n    constructor(address token0_, uint112 reserve0_, uint112 reserve1_) {\n        _token0 = token0_;\n        _reserve0 = reserve0_;\n        _reserve1 = reserve1_;\n        _blockTimestampLast = uint32(block.timestamp);\n    }\n\n    function setReserves(uint112 r0, uint112 r1) external {\n        _reserve0 = r0;\n        _reserve1 = r1;\n    }\n\n    function setBlockTimestampLast(uint32 ts) external {\n        _blockTimestampLast = ts;\n    }\n\n    function token0() external view returns (address) {\n        return _token0;\n    }\n\n    function getReserves() external view returns (uint112, uint112, uint32) {\n        return (_reserve0, _reserve1, _blockTimestampLast);\n    }\n\n    function price0CumulativeLast() external pure returns (uint256) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    function price1CumulativeLast() external pure returns (uint256) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract UniswapPriceOracleTest is Test {\n    function testValidatePriceTwapCollapsesToSpot() public {\n        MockUniswapV2 pair = new MockUniswapV2(address(1), 1e18, 2e18);\n        UniswapPriceOracle oracle = new UniswapPriceOracle(address(1), 1e18, address(pair));\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1);\n        bool ok = oracle.validatePrice(0);\n        assertTrue(ok);\n        uint256 priceBefore = oracle.getPrice();\n        pair.setReserves(uint112(100e18), uint112(10_000e18));\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1);\n        uint256 priceAfter = oracle.getPrice();\n        assertTrue(priceAfter != priceBefore);\n        ok = oracle.validatePrice(0);\n        assertTrue(ok);\n    }\n}\n```",
